{
  "id": "COMPOUND:38271 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Sasanquasaponin I is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Sasanquasaponin I acts as a target for multiple compounds, which in turn target the choline transporter. Specifically, Microtubule-associated protein 1B, a known target of Sasanquasaponin I, is also a target of other compounds, including Petroraspailyne B1 and (+)-(8S,8'R)-4-hydroxy-3,3',4',5'-tetramethoxylignan. These compounds all ultimately lead to the activation of the High-affinity choline transporter. This suggests a potential mechanism where Sasanquasaponin I may influence the activity of the choline transporter through the modulation of its upstream targets. The consistent involvement of the choline transporter across multiple pathways indicates a possible role in cellular processes that are regulated by Sasanquasaponin I, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
